  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be defined as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Then, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></munder><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to ________.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
